# Integration test: Apple HD SC Setup accepts an Apple-branded 230 MB drive.
#
# The Copland D11E4 installer refuses any target volume under 230 MB, and it
# also refuses a disk that Apple's own formatter never touched (its rule 207,
# "Check for Secondary Ldr Partn", looks for the driver partition Drive Setup
# writes).  Before HD500SC existed the catalog topped out at 169 MB, so no
# emulated drive could satisfy both.  This test pins the fix end to end:
# Apple's formatter must see the drive, offer Initialize, and complete.
#
# What makes the drive acceptable is MODE SENSE page 0x30 returning
# "APPLE COMPUTER, INC." (scsi.c) — not the INQUIRY vendor/product ID.  A
# regression there shows up here as a greyed-out Initialize button.
#
# Mouse timing mirrors se30-format-hd: 5M cycles after a move for VBL
# propagation, then 1M-cycle click phases.

# HD230SC = Quantum ProDrive LPS 240S, 479,350 blocks, the Apple 230 MB SKU —
# the smallest catalog entry above the installer's floor.  Formatting it here
# yields a 479,254-block (245,378,048 byte) HFS volume, which clears 230 MB
# whether the installer means decimal MB or MiB.
assert storage.hd_create("${$WORK_DIR}/apple230.img", "HD230SC") "hd_create HD230SC failed"
assert storage.path_size("${$WORK_DIR}/apple230.img") == 245427200 "HD230SC wrong image size"

machine.scsi.attach_hd "$WORK_DIR/apple230.img" 0

# The INQUIRY identity the catalog entry is supposed to present.
assert machine.scsi.device[0].vendor == "QUANTUM " "unexpected SCSI vendor"
assert machine.scsi.device[0].product == "LP240S GM240S01X" "unexpected SCSI product"
assert machine.scsi.device[0].revision == "6.3 " "unexpected SCSI revision"

# Boot to the Finder desktop (SE/30, 8 MB RAM).  The drive is unformatted, so
# it must NOT mount here — only HD SC Setup should be able to touch it.
scheduler.run 80000000
machine.screen.match desktop.png

# Double-click "Disk Tools" to open the floppy
machine.adb.mouse.move 480 55 "global"
scheduler.run 5000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false
scheduler.run 50000000
machine.screen.match floppy.png

# Double-click Apple HD SC Setup
machine.adb.mouse.move 167 83 "global"
scheduler.run 5000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false
scheduler.run 50000000

# THE ACCEPTANCE CHECK.  A drive the formatter rejects reports "This program
# cannot be used on the selected device" with Initialize disabled; an accepted
# one reports "The disk is uninitialized..." with Initialize enabled.
machine.screen.match ready.png

# Initialize
machine.adb.mouse.move 167 115 "global"
scheduler.run 5000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false
scheduler.run 5000000
machine.screen.match confirm.png

# Confirm "Init" in the erase-warning dialog
machine.adb.mouse.move 360 190 "global"
scheduler.run 5000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false

# Writing the driver, partition map and volume across 479,350 blocks
scheduler.run 800000000

# "Please name this volume." — accept the default
machine.adb.mouse.move 200 180 "global"
scheduler.run 5000000
machine.adb.mouse.click true
scheduler.run 1000000
machine.adb.mouse.click false
scheduler.run 80000000

# "Disk initialization successfully completed." plus the now-mounted volume,
# and Update/Partition/Test enabled — all three only appear for a drive the
# formatter considers a supported Apple mechanism.
machine.screen.match done.png

quit
